 "stimulus_html": "Find the percent in the following:",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 516541,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Total is 40, percent of the total is 25",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The formula relating the total (base), the percent in decimal form, and the part (amount) is</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"part = percent \\times total\"></span>.</p>\n<p>25 is what percent of 40?</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"25 = percent \\times 40\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{{25}}{{40}} = \\frac{{percent \\times \\cancel{{40}}}}{{\\cancel{{40}}}}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"0.625 = percent\"></span></p>\n<p>To convert the number <i>x</i> from decimal form to percent, multiply <i>x</i> by 100 and place a percent sign, %, after the number: (<i>x</i> × 100)%.</p>\n<p>0.625 = 62.5%</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "62.5%"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 516542,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Total is 730, percent of the total is 292",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The formula relating the total (base), the percent in decimal form, and the part (amount) is</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"part = percent \\times total\"></span>.</p>\n<p>292 is what percent of 730?</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"292 = percent \\times 730\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{{292}}{{730}} = \\frac{{percent \\times \\cancel{{292}}}}{{\\cancel{{292}}}}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"0.4 = percent\"></span></p>\n<p>To convert the number <i>x</i> from decimal form to percent, multiply <i>x</i> by 100 and place a percent sign, %, after the number: (<i>x</i> × 100)%.</p>\n<p>0.40 = 40%</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "40%"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
